# Task Dashboard Usage Guidelines

## Task Structure

- **Task Organization**
  - Tasks are hierarchically organized with main tasks and subtasks
  - Each task has a unique ID (numeric for main tasks, dotted for subtasks)
  - Dependencies are tracked between main tasks
  - Status tracking with visual indicators (✅ done, 🔄 pending)

- **Required Task Fields**
  ```json
  {
    "id": "unique_id",
    "title": "Clear, descriptive title",
    "status": "pending|done",
    "priority": "high|medium|low",
    "dependencies": [task_ids],
    "description": "Brief overview",
    "details": "Implementation details",
    "subtasks": []
  }
  ```

## Dashboard Commands

- **Basic Usage**
  ```bash
  # View task summary
  go run project/tasks/dashboard.go
  
  # View detailed task information
  go run project/tasks/dashboard.go --detailed
  ```

- **Visual Indicators**
  - ✅ Completed tasks/subtasks
  - 🔄 Pending tasks/subtasks
  - 📌 Task markers in detailed view
  - 🚀 Project header

## Development Workflow

- **Task Selection Process**
  1. Run dashboard to view current progress
  2. Check dependency chain (tasks with no pending dependencies)
  3. Select highest priority available task
  4. Review detailed task information
  5. Begin implementation of subtasks in order

- **Progress Tracking**
  - Monitor completion percentages for both main tasks and subtasks
  - Update task status after completing implementation
  - Verify all subtasks are complete before marking main task as done
  - Keep task.json synchronized with implementation progress

- **Task Dependencies**
  - Respect task dependency order during development
  - Only start tasks when all dependencies are marked as done
  - Update dependency list if new dependencies are discovered
  - Document any changes to the dependency chain

## Agentic AI Integration

- **AI Task Context**
  - Include task ID in all AI interactions
  - Reference specific subtasks when discussing implementation
  - Provide task details and description for context
  - Maintain task status alignment with AI progress

- **Implementation Guidelines**
  - Break down complex tasks into manageable subtasks
  - Update task status after each significant milestone
  - Document any deviations from original task plan
  - Keep AI informed of task dependencies and constraints

- **Progress Reporting**
  - Use dashboard output to track AI development progress
  - Include task metrics in development reports
  - Document completion of subtasks and main tasks
  - Track overall project velocity

## Best Practices

- **Task Management**
  - Keep tasks.json up to date with current progress
  - Use meaningful task titles and descriptions
  - Maintain clear dependency relationships
  - Document implementation details thoroughly

- **Status Updates**
  - Update task status immediately after completion
  - Verify all subtasks before updating main task status
  - Include relevant commit hashes in task details
  - Document any blockers or issues

- **Code Organization**
  - Align code structure with task hierarchy
  - Use task IDs in branch names and commits
  - Maintain traceability between tasks and code
  - Document relationships between tasks and components

## Task Review Process

- **Completion Criteria**
  - All subtasks implemented and tested
  - Code documentation complete
  - Tests passing
  - No pending dependencies
  - Implementation matches task details

- **Review Steps**
  1. Run dashboard with --detailed flag
  2. Review all subtask implementations
  3. Verify dependency completion
  4. Check overall progress metrics
  5. Update task status after successful review

## Troubleshooting

- **Common Issues**
  - Mismatched task status
  - Incomplete dependency chain
  - Missing subtask implementation
  - Incorrect progress calculation

- **Resolution Steps**
  1. Verify task.json structure
  2. Check dependency relationships
  3. Review implementation status
  4. Update task status accordingly
  5. Re-run dashboard to verify fixes 